Now I see the full picture. Let me check `CurrentUserService` to understand when `IsRegistered` returns true.

Looking at `RegisteredUserHandler`:
```csharp
if (_currentUserService.IsRegistered)
{
    context.Succeed(requirement);
}
```

And `AuthEndpoints.cs`'s `/me` endpoint:
```csharp
auth.MapGet("/me", ...).RequireAuthorization("RegisteredUser");
```

The `RegisteredUser` policy requires:
