content.text:
Two changes, explained concisely:

**`useCurrentUser.ts`** — `isLoading` now uses `isPending` (TanStack Query v5). In v5, `isLoading = isPending && isFetching`, which is `false` when the query is paused (e.g., browser hasn't reported online yet to the network observer). `isPending` correctly means "no data available yet" regardless of fetch status, so `ProtectedRoute` always waits for the query to settle before rendering.

**`App.tsx`** — `isNotRegistered` is checked first (403 → `/not-registered`), then `isUnauthenticated || isError` covers 401 AND any other failure (network error, 502 from Vite proxy if API is slow to respond, etc.). Previously, any non-401/403 error silently fell through to render the board.

The snippet fix for the test:

```ts
// No code change needed in the test itself — the fix is in ProtectedRoute.
// The fresh browser.newContext() has no cookie → API returns 401 →
// isError=true, isUnauthenticated=true → Navigate to="/signin"  ✅
```

